<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexandru Lăpușneanu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1568">1568</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexandru Lăpușneanu was prince of Moldavia from 1552 to 1561 and again from 1564 to 1568. Known for his cruelty towards the boyars, he moved the capital from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suceava">Suceava</a> to Iași and founded the Slatina Monastery. He is the subject of a famous Romanian novella by Costache Negruzzi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexandru-lapusneanu.jpg" alt="Alexandru Lăpușneanu" width="320" height="546" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lapusneanu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
